{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/6043","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:57:13.026602+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"Should be fixed in latest. Try building top of tree from source.","created_at":"2025-03-13T16:45:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/triton-lang/triton/issues/6043#issuecomment-2721953836","id":2721953836,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/6043","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAWaHXs6iPbgs","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":1,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":1,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/2721953836/reactions"},"updated_at":"2025-03-13T16:45:52Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/comments/2721953836","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24322263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ThomasRaoux","id":24322263,"login":"ThomasRaoux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzIyMjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux","user_view_type":"public"}}],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Bug Description\nWhen using `uint8` indices for pointer arithmetic, the indices are incorrectly interpreted as `int8` (negative above 127).\n\n### Minimal Reproducible Example\nHere `uint8` indices in the range [0, 255] are used in loading.\n\n```python\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\nimport torch\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef pointer_uint8_bug_kernel(\n    out_ptr,\n    out_wrong_ptr,\n    src_ptr,\n    numel: tl.constexpr,\n    BLOCK_SIZE: tl.constexpr,\n):\n    start_idx = tl.program_id(0) * BLOCK_SIZE\n\n    src_indices = tl.cast(tl.arange(0, 256), tl.uint8)\n    tl.static_assert(src_indices.dtype is tl.uint8)\n\n    # Incorrect: src_indices interpreted as int8 instead of uint8\n    out_wrong = tl.load(src_ptr + src_indices, mask=src_indices < BLOCK_SIZE)\n\n    out_correct = tl.load(\n        src_ptr + tl.cast(src_indices, tl.uint32), mask=src_indices < BLOCK_SIZE\n    )\n\n    # Store results\n    out_indices = start_idx + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_SIZE)\n    tl.store(out_ptr + out_indices, out_correct, mask=out_indices < numel)\n    tl.store(out_wrong_ptr + out_indices, out_wrong, mask=out_indices < numel)\n\n\ndef test_pointer_uint8_bug():\n    numel = 192\n    BLOCK_SIZE = 256\n    BEFORE_SRC_VAL = 11\n\n    data = torch.arange(-128, numel, dtype=torch.float32, device=\"cuda\")\n    data[:128] = BEFORE_SRC_VAL\n    src = data[128:]  # values 0 to numel\n\n    out = torch.empty(numel, dtype=torch.float32, device=\"cuda\")\n    out_wrong = torch.empty_like(out)\n\n    grid = lambda meta: (triton.cdiv(numel, meta[\"BLOCK_SIZE\"]),)\n    pointer_uint8_bug_kernel[grid](\n        out_ptr=out,\n        out_wrong_ptr=out_wrong,\n        src_ptr=src,\n        numel=numel,\n        BLOCK_SIZE=BLOCK_SIZE,\n    )\n\n    assert torch.all(out == src)\n    assert torch.all(out_wrong[:128] == src[:128])  # correct up to index 128\n    assert torch.all(out_wrong[128:] == BEFORE_SRC_VAL)  # incorrect after index 128, memory before of src\n    print(out_wrong)\n\n\ntest_pointer_uint8_bug()\n```\n\n### Expected Behavior\n- Indices 0-255 should access memory locations at offsets 0-255 from the source pointer.\n- The loaded arrays `out_wrong` and `out` should be equal.\n\n### Actual Behavior\n- Indices 0-127 work correctly.\n- Indices 128-255 are interpreted as negative numbers (-128 to -1).\n- This causes reading from wrong memory locations before the source pointer.\n\n### Workaround\nA workaround is to convert the `uint8` indices to some integer type with more bits:\n\n```python\nout_correct = tl.load(src_ptr + tl.cast(src_indices, tl.uint32), mask=src_indices < BLOCK_SIZE)\n```\n\n### Comments\nI encountered this bug when implementing dequantization.\n\n### Environment details\n\nTriton 3.2.0\nCUDA 12.7\nNVIDIA RTX A4500\nPyTorch 2.6.0+cu124","closed_at":"2025-03-13T16:45:52Z","closed_by":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24322263?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ThomasRaoux","id":24322263,"login":"ThomasRaoux","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI0MzIyMjYz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ThomasRaoux","user_view_type":"public"},"comments":1,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/6043/comments","created_at":"2025-02-27T14:39:26Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/triton-lang/triton/issues/6043/events","html_url":"https://github.